# Design validation

After UI exists, check it. Do not write UI in this check.

Design is **validate-only on purpose**. There is no spec-commit gate. Figma (if present) or existing screens, components, and tokens plus the house craft bar already are the spec.

## When to skip

Skip for backend-only work, TDD logic with no UI, docs-only work, or throwaway spikes. Say that you skipped the design check and why.

Do not start this check during TDD Red or Green of logic tests. Do not start it if the implementer is Stuck.

## Workflow

The parent agent orchestrates. Subagents do not commit.

1. **UI exists** — A screen, component, layout, or motion change is in the tree (TDD was skipped for polish, or Green also changed UI).
2. **Lock the source (read only)** — If a Figma URL or node is present, Figma is first. Load `figma-design-to-code` and call `get_design_context`. Do not override Figma with taste. If there is no Figma, use existing screens, components, and tokens in the project, plus the house craft bar (`ui-craft`, `review-animations` STANDARDS). If the UI is Expo or React Native, also load `animate-expo` for thread, gesture, and haptic rules. Load `emil-design-eng` only when the user names it. It is not a second bar.
3. **Check** — Delegate to the `design-verifier` subagent. It does not change UI. It does not commit. It does not loop.
4. **Report** — Treat **Approved** or **Approved with reservations** as done for look. **Rejected** means fix UI, then check again. At most **2** fix-and-recheck cycles. After that, stop and ask the user. Do not loop.

If Figma is missing and existing screens or tokens are not enough, say what is missing. Do not stop to write and commit a spec file.

## Rules

- `verifier` checks that it works. `design-verifier` checks that it matches the design source and the craft bar.
- Tiny pixel diffs are not a fail if tokens and structure match, unless Figma is strict.
- Motion and polish use the house craft bar (`ui-craft`, `review-animations` STANDARDS). Do not invent a second set of values. Do not treat `emil-design-eng` as a second bar.
- Never auto-commit. Subagents never commit.
